=== Quant-Arena spirit (arXiv:2610.30113) ===
freeze factor list AFTER IS loop; evaluate sealed hold-out ONCE; no peeking / re-mining.
frozen_kept=['noise_A', 'slow_lag1']
sealed_OOS_IC agent=+0.0161 vs honest=+0.0154
paper punchline (verified): top-scored sealed-2024 run ~10.7% ARR vs ~17.1% equal-weight — see later section.

=== mock Lopez-Lira & Tang (2023) headline sentiment (offline) ===
paper: GPT scores on post-knowledge-cutoff headlines predict reactions/drift (arXiv:2304.07619).
here: synthetic 'headlines' → mock_sentiment in [-1,1]; NO ChatGPT call.
mock_sentiment_PIT     post_cutoff mean_CS_IC=+0.0011 t=0.12 net_SR=-12.015 DSR(N=2)=0.000
mock_sentiment_LEAK    post_cutoff mean_CS_IC=+0.6740 t=125.99 net_SR=48.362 DSR(N=2)=1.000
teach: LEAK foil inflates IC (cutoff/memorization analogue); PIT mock is the honest path.

=== Chain-of-Alpha (arXiv:2508.06312) — WITHDRAWN (live banner wording) ===
arXiv banner: "This paper has been withdrawn by Lang Cao"
arXiv admin comment: "This version has been removed by arXiv administrators as the submitter did not have the rights to agree to the license at the time of submission"
DROP detailed dual-chain claims; do not depend on an unstable PDF.
Prefer stable cites: RD-Agent(Q), AlphaAgent, LLM+MCTS, Quant-Arena.

=== Quant-Arena negative leaderboard punchline (arXiv:2610.30113, verified) ===
Protocol: research on 2022–2023 with <=5 candidates; freeze ONE strategy; sealed year 2024 once.
Verified punchline: no model's *best-scoring* sealed-2024 run beat equal-weight.
Best top-scored run: GPT-6 Astra ARR ~ 10.7% vs gross equal-weight market ARR ~ 17.1% (excess ~ -6.3 pp).
Note: 1/38 configs (Sol medium) ARR 18.4% above EW — but that is NOT the model's best total-score row; not advantage evidence.
Teach: sealed hold-out + costs can turn a leaderboard into a caution, not a green light.

=== AlphaAgent originality / complexity / hypothesis alignment (arXiv:2502.16789) ===
cite: https://github.com/RndmVariableQ/AlphaAgent
Without originality/complexity/hypothesis-alignment regularizers, LLM factors homogenize -> crowded -> decay.
  homogen_candidate max Jaccard vs zoo = 1.000 (high -> crowded / low originality)
  novel_candidate    max Jaccard vs zoo = 0.545 (lower -> more original structurally)
Still required after any agent mine: purge / DSR(N) / sealed OOS — originality != edge.

=== Parametric look-ahead (weights remember the future) — PROBLEM (arXiv:2605.24564) ===
If an LLM was pretrained through year T, a backtest on years < T can use memorized outcomes
inside the *weights* — invisible to PIT data audits. Teach: post-cutoff / sealed-year only for claims.
FinCAD decoding mitigation = NAME-ONLY footnote (recipe out of scope for this course).

=== CogAlpha (arXiv:2511.18850) — NAME-ONLY map ===
Code-based evolutionary LLM alpha mining next to RD-Agent / AlphaAgent.
Shared traps: trial inflation, homogenization, leaky eval, paper metrics != sealed costs/DSR.
Out of scope here: Deep RL / FinRL-as-alpha / HFT recipes / options MM.

=== limitations / failure modes (must-read) ===
- LLM training cutoff / memorization: scores on pre-cutoff headlines are not forecasts.
- Agent loops multiply trials → DSR needs explicit N; paper metrics ≠ your OOS edge.
- IS keep rules (IC>threshold) overfit; sealed hold-out must stay sealed.
- Formula banks / CoT traces can look interpretable while mining noise.
- Chain-of-Alpha withdrawn (Lang Cao + admin license comment): do not rely on unstable PDFs.
- LLM factors homogenize without originality/complexity/hypothesis constraints (AlphaAgent).
- Parametric look-ahead: weights can memorize in-cutoff outcomes (FinCAD PROBLEM; sealed-year only).
- Marketing: 'AI hedge fund / always-profitable LLM' claims fail Quant-Arena-style sealed tests.

