=== five LLM-finance sins + structural validity (arXiv:2602.14233) ===
  sin#1 look_ahead: future info in weights/RAG at historical t
  sin#2 survivorship: delisted/failed names silently dropped
  sin#3 narrative: fluent story not supported by evidence at t
  sin#4 objective: confident completion rewarded over calibrated abstention
  sin#5 cost: gross metrics with zero friction / zero inference cost
structural_validity checklist (pass/fail before deployment claim):
  [GATE] temporal_sanitation: FAIL if any prompt/RAG/tool uses post-t info
  [GATE] dynamic_universe: FAIL if universe is end-of-sample survivors only
  [GATE] rationale_robustness: FAIL if explanations are untested decoration
  [GATE] epistemic_calibration: FAIL if forced guess with no abstention scored
  [GATE] realistic_costs_latency: FAIL if primary metric is frictionless gross
paper: among 164 conf papers, no single bias discussed in >28%; look-ahead ~26.8%

=== long-horizon LLM timing under bias-mitigated eval (arXiv:2505.07078 FINSABER) ===
cite: Li/Kim/Cucuringu/Ma — FinMem/FinAgent-style short selective windows overstate skill
toy foil: selective 6m window SR inflated vs 20y-like pooled mean under same rule
selective_best_~6m_SR≈4.079  full_sample_SR≈0.191  buy_hold_SR≈-0.027
delta_selective_minus_full≈+3.889  <-- short windows + symbol pick inflate
DEBUNK: FinMem/FinAgent-style marketing on <1y / <10 names is not long-run evidence.
paper composite setups: B&H often beats FinMem/FinAgent on risk-adjusted metrics.

=== OpenPM protocol spirit (arXiv:2608.09988) — audit, not PnL ===
OpenPM: availability-gated PIT eval + contamination certificate + cost curve + mandate critic
teach: returns without leakage/cost/mandate audits are upper bounds — not validated alpha
NAME use: adopt audit artifacts; do not ship OpenPM PnL as a strategy claim

=== CLQT: diagnose process, don't rank period Sharpe (arXiv:2606.29771) ===
cite: Qu & Chen — CLQT closed-loop cost-aware strategy-consistent benchmark
stating-vs-doing gap: agents' allocations fail to follow their own stated analysis
capability leader ≠ Sharpe leader; campaign Sharpes are NOT curriculum edge
CLQT_checklist:
  [Y] PiT TimeGate — hard gate: no future timestamps in tools/memory
  [Y] multi-component costs — commission+spread+impact+financing modeled
  [P] strategy consistency score — stated thesis vs executed weights audited
  [P] sealed audit hash chain — recompute-verifiable DecisionRound
  [Y] capability axes vs Sharpe board — diagnose Coherence/Acuity/...; do not crown period Sharpe
REJECT: pasting CLQT campaign Sharpes (e.g. 2.99 / 9.82 artifacts) as course alpha

=== AQuA sealed sandbox PROTOCOL ONLY (arXiv:2608.12841) ===
cite: Guo et al. — recursive self-improving quant research agents
structural idea: freeze splits/features/labels/evaluator; agent may only emit constrained DSL / config diffs
bridge: same spirit as ml-leakage-control sealed hold-out + fixed evaluator
REJECT BOX: do NOT teach Part II IC/+0.0843 or Sharpe +2.50 as curriculum edge / deployable alpha
AQuA_protocol_gates: splits_frozen=Y features_frozen=Y labels_frozen=Y evaluator_frozen=Y

=== Execution-assumption recoverability (arXiv:2606.08285 Yao&Zheng) ===
cite: PRISMA-ScR audit — architecture reported more than fill timing/costs/universe/artifacts
capstone_recoverability_Y_P_NR:
  PiT / availability times: Y
  split dates train/val/test: Y
  fill timing (next-open vs same-close): P
  costs + turnover: P
  universe construction: NR
  artifacts (code/prompts/model versions): P
teach: a Y means reconstructable from public evidence — not that the assumption is realistic or profitable
research_log_row: date | paper | PiT | splits | fill | costs | universe | artifacts | next_action
